course: dictionary
lesson: 14041
title: Manual: by hand, or a book of instructions
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Manual is a word with two jobs. As an adjective, it describes work done by hand, with a person's effort, not by a machine. «Sam did the manual work of digging the garden.» Sam used his own hands and muscles, not a digger.
explain: As a noun, a manual is a book of instructions that tells you how to use or fix something. «Before you switch on the new printer, read the manual.» The word instructions is the clue: the manual tells you what to do, step by step.
explain: Look at the words around manual to decide which job it does. If it comes before a noun, like manual work or manual skills, it is usually an adjective. If it is the thing you read or use, it is usually a noun. Then try the swap test: does «by hand» fit in the sentence? If it does, manual is the adjective.
fact: Manual can be an adjective or a noun; as a noun, the plural is manuals.
fact: «Manual» as an adjective means done by hand or by a person's effort, not by a machine.
fact: «Manual» as a noun means a book of instructions for using or fixing something.
fact: A manual car has gears that the driver changes by hand; in the US this is called a stick shift.
fact: Useful phrases: «user manual», «manual work», and «manual override».
exercise: «Sam did the manual work of digging the garden.» What does manual mean here? | Done by a machine | *Done by hand, with a person's effort | Done at night | Done in a hurry
exercise: «Before you switch on the new printer, read the manual.» What is a manual in this sentence? | A kind of printer | A type of game | A machine that makes paper | *A book of instructions
exercise: Mia's car is a manual, so she changes the gears herself. What does manual car mean? | A very fast car | A car with no wheels | *A car where the driver changes the gears by hand | A car that drives itself
test: In «Ella has good manual skills, like cutting and sewing», what does manual describe? | *Skills done with the hands | A book of rules | Ella's bike | Ella's computer
test: Which of these is a manual? | A torch | A tent | *A book telling you how to set up a tent | A rucksack
exam: Which sentence uses manual as an adjective? | «Read the manual before you start.» | «The manual was lost under the sofa.» | *«He carried the bricks with manual effort, not a machine.»
